# Temporary ignores for OS CVEs whose Debian fix (python3.11 3.11.2-6+deb12u8)
# is published in the security tracker but not yet installable from the
# bookworm mirrors at image build time (apt still serves deb12u7).
# Added 2026-07-12 (PR #210). REMOVE both entries once a rebuild picks up
# deb12u8 — verify with: docker run --rm gantry-runtime:scan dpkg -l python3.11
CVE-2026-4224
CVE-2026-6100

# CVE-2026-16633 (pdfjs-dist < 6.2.108, arbitrary JS on malicious PDF).
# The ACTUAL installed pdfjs-dist is 6.2.108 everywhere — the direct dependency
# is bumped and an overrides.pdfjs-dist = ^6.2.108 forces the transitive copy
# (officeparser) to dedupe to 6.2.108 (verify: `npm ls pdfjs-dist --all`).
# Trivy still reports 5.6.205 because it reads officeparser@6.1.1's DECLARED
# exact-pin ("pdfjs-dist": "5.6.205") from its package.json rather than the
# resolved install; npm overrides cannot rewrite a dependency's own manifest,
# and no officeparser release yet declares a fixed pdfjs (latest 7.5.1 declares
# 6.1.200, still < 6.2.108). We never route PDFs to officeparser (office docs
# only), so its pdfjs path is never exercised regardless. Added 2026-08-08.
# REMOVE once officeparser ships a release declaring pdfjs-dist >= 6.2.108.
CVE-2026-16633
